Description: Only the library in src/ is configured and built
 The packages ship only the library, its header, pkg-config file and
 autoconf macro. Without doc/ and tests/ in configure.ac and SUBDIRS,
 automake does not read the manual or the test makefiles. Without
 src/versioninfo.rc and src/ksba-config, configure does not read their
 templates. ber-dump is not built: the packages do not ship it. Only
 ber-dump and the tests used gnulib's gl/, so gl/ is not configured.
 m4/Makefile only lists the macros for make dist, so it is not
 configured either.
 In foreign mode automake needs no AUTHORS, ChangeLog, INSTALL, NEWS,
 README or COPYING. AB_INIT only logs build details, so autobuild.m4 is
 not used.
Author: The Blueberry Pie OS Authors
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-04
